The source code of Junkyard Draft is published so that anyone can read how the game, its
simulation and its replay verifier work, check that the verified leaderboards do what the
fairness policy says, run the game for themselves and contribute improvements. It is not
free software: the rights below are the only ones granted.

1. Permitted. Subject to the conditions in section 3 you may, free of charge:
   a. view, download and keep copies of this repository;
   b. build and run the game, the verifier and the tools on machines you control, for
      personal, educational or development use, including a verifier that only you and the
      people you invite can reach;
   c. modify the code for those uses and keep your modifications private;
   d. submit modifications, bug reports and other contributions to the official repository
      (section 4);
   e. quote reasonable excerpts of the code with attribution, for commentary, teaching or
      review.

2. Not permitted without the copyright holder's prior written permission:
   a. distributing the game, the verifier, the tools, builds or installers, modified or not,
      to the public, including hosting a playable copy on a public web site or app store;
   b. operating a publicly reachable instance of the verifier or a leaderboard presented as
      Junkyard Draft or as connected to it;
   c. commercial use of any kind, including advertising, paid access and bundling;
   d. use of the name "Junkyard Draft", the logo, the wordmark, the artwork, the sound
      effects, the music and the share-card designs (the "brand assets"), except to refer
      to the game truthfully. The brand assets are not licensed under this document at all.

3. Conditions. Every copy you keep or share under section 1 carries this licence and the
   copyright notice unchanged. You do not remove or alter notices in the files. You do not
   present a modified version as the original or imply the copyright holder's endorsement.

4. Contributions. By submitting a contribution to the official repository you license it
   to the copyright holder under these same terms and, in addition, grant the copyright
   holder a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free right to use, modify, relicense and
   distribute it as part of Junkyard Draft under any licence, including open-source
   licences. You confirm that you have the right to make that grant. You keep your own
   copyright and may use your contribution elsewhere.

5. Third-party components keep their own licences (see package.json and the vendor
   directory, notably Phaser under the MIT licence). Nothing here restricts them.

6. No warranty. The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose
   and non-infringement. In no event shall the copyright holder be liable for any claim,
   damages or other liability arising from the software or its use.

7. Termination. The rights in section 1 end automatically if you breach this licence. They
   are restored if you cure the breach within 30 days of becoming aware of it, unless the
   holder tells you otherwise. Sections 2, 4, 6 and 7 survive termination.

8. Governing law: the law of the copyright holder's place of residence, the United States,
   without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules.

Why this licence and not an open-source one: the engine may be relicensed later (the
contribution grant in section 4 keeps that possible), but the name, the art and the hosted
leaderboards are what make the game one place to play, and the holder wants a single public
instance while it is small. Questions: contact@junkyarddraft.com.
